Note (1): The ordering in Bintype does not account for primary/secondary
  designations. Binary types as follows:
   ???? = Both no colours (1 040 occurrences)
   MS?? = One main sequence, one no colours (378 877 occurrences)
   WD?? = One white dwarf, one no colours (646 occurrences)
   MSMS = Both main sequence (1 412 903 occurrences)
   WDWD = Both white dwarf (1 565 occurrences)
   WDMS = One white dwarf, one main sequence (22 563 occurrences)
Note (2): We denote the  KDE-estimated density of chance alignments at a point
   vector_x_ in the 7D parameter space as N_chance_(vector_x_) and that of
   binary candidates as N_candidate_(vector_x_). R is the ratio of the two
   quantities.
